  GarbhSacredStory('Krishna’s Big Umbrella', 'Bhagavata Purana', [2, 3], 'A big storm came to the village with lots of rain and wind. Everyone was scared. But Krishna simply lifted a big hill with his tiny finger, holding it up like a giant umbrella. Everyone stood under it, safe, dry, and happy, knowing that Krishna was looking after them.', 'You are always protected, safe, and looked after.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Churning for the Good', 'Puranas', [2], 'The gods were mixing the big ocean to find something special. At first, things were messy and hard. But they didn\'t stop. They kept going, and soon, the most wonderful things came out of the water. They learned that if you are patient, good things will happen.', 'Good things come to those who wait and stay calm.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Ganesha’s World', 'Shiva Purana', [1, 2], 'Ganesha was in a race around the whole world. While others ran fast, Ganesha simply walked around his parents with love. He told them, "You are my whole world." He won the race because he knew that love is the most important thing.', 'Your family and your love are your whole world.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Savitri’s Brave Wish', 'Mahabharata', [3], 'Princess Savitri was told that her husband had only a short time to live. When the God of Time came to take him away, she didn\'t cry or give up. Instead, she walked right alongside him, speaking so beautifully and wisely about love and kindness. The God was so amazed by her clever mind and brave heart that he gave her husband his life back.', 'Love and a clever mind can change your destiny.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Dadhichi’s Gift of Strength', 'Puranas', [3], 'The good guys in heaven needed a special, strong shield to defeat a giant trouble-maker. Only something made from the strongest, purest material could do it. A kind and wise teacher named Dadhichi happily sat down in peace and offered his own strong bones to help make the shield, saving the whole world with his kindness.', 'True strength is using what you have to help others.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Little Markandeya’s Shield', 'Puranas', [1, 2], 'A young boy named Markandeya was told he wouldn\'t live a long life. Instead of being scared, he sat down, cleared his mind of all worries, and sang a peaceful song of protection. His heart was so pure and still that a bright energy shielded him from all harm, granting him health and a long, happy life.', 'When your mind is peaceful and still, fear cannot touch you.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Ekalavya’s Quiet Practice', 'Mahabharata', [2], 'Ekalavya wanted to learn how to use a bow and arrow, but the famous teacher was too busy for him. He didn\'t complain. He went into the quiet woods, made a small clay model of the teacher to inspire him, and practiced every single day with love. Because he worked so hard on his own, he became the best archer in the land.', 'If you believe in yourself and practice, nothing can stop you.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Ashtavakra’s Wise Words', 'Mahabharata', [3], 'Ashtavakra was a boy born with a crooked body. When he walked into a room full of proud scholars, they laughed at how he looked. He laughed back and said, "You are looking at my outer shell, but you are completely missing the beautiful, perfect mind inside." The scholars went quiet, realizing the boy was wiser than all of them.', 'Who you are on the inside is what truly matters.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Tiny Fish that Grew', 'Puranas', [1], 'A kind king found a tiny, fragile fish in his hands that asked for shelter. The king put it in a small bowl, but the fish grew so fast it needed a jar, then a pond, and then a whole ocean! The fish turned out to be a helper who guided the king\'s boat through a big storm, keeping all the seeds of life safe.', 'Even the tiniest spark can grow into something magnificent.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Steady Tortoise', 'Puranas', [2, 3], 'A group of friends was trying to stir a massive bowl of milk to find a hidden treasure, but the heavy mixing rod started sinking into the soft mud. Seeing this, a giant, gentle tortoise swam underneath and held the heavy weight steady on his strong shell, providing the perfect support so everyone could finish their work.', 'Be the steady support that helps everyone around you stay calm.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The King and the Little Dove', 'Mahabharata', [2], 'A scared little dove flew into a king\'s lap, hiding from a hungry hawk. The king promised to keep the dove safe. When the hawk complained it had no food, the king offered a piece of his own food instead of giving up the dove. He showed that a true leader always protects the weak, no matter what.', 'Always stand up for those who need your help.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Coming Together as One Light', 'Devi Mahatmyam', [2, 3], 'When a huge problem threatened the world, no single person was strong enough to fix it. So, all the wise beings gathered around and put their brightest, most beautiful energies together into one place. From that combined light, a powerful mother protector appeared and easily brought peace back to the land.', 'When we bring our best energies together, we can fix anything.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Quiet Tree Transformation', 'Puranas', [2], 'A man who used to be very angry and mean decided he wanted a peaceful life. He sat down under a tree and focused his entire mind on one beautiful, quiet thought. He sat so still for so long that an anthill grew over him like a blanket. When he finally opened his eyes, his heart was completely soft, kind, and full of peace.', 'Quiet time and good thoughts can completely change your heart.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Rama & the Little Squirrel', 'Ramayana', [1, 2], 'While building a massive stone bridge across the sea, a tiny squirrel wanted to help. The big monkeys laughed because the squirrel could only carry tiny grains of sand in its fur. But Rama picked up the squirrel gently, stroked its back with three fingers, and said that its small, loving effort was just as important as the heavy rocks.', 'No helper is too small, and every kind effort matters.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Chariot and the Horses', 'Bhagavad Gita', [2, 3], 'Krishna explained to Arjuna that our body is like a beautiful wooden carriage pulled by five strong horses. The horses are our senses, and the driver holding the reins is our clever mind. When the driver is calm, awake, and gentle, the horses walk beautifully and safely down the right path.', 'When you guide your thoughts gently, life goes smoothly.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Shabari’s Sweet Berries', 'Ramayana', [1, 2], 'An old woman named Shabari lived in a small forest hut, waiting patiently for years to welcome Rama. Every morning, she picked wild berries for him, taking a tiny bite of each one first to make sure it was perfectly sweet and not sour. When Rama finally arrived, he happily ate them all because they were filled with pure, honest love.', 'Patience and true love make the simplest things special.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Elephant\'s Gentle Prayer', 'Bhagavata Purana', [2, 3], 'A mighty king elephant named Gajendra went for a swim in a lake, but a large crocodile caught his foot and wouldn\'t let go. He fought hard for a long time until he was completely tired out. Finally, he stopped fighting, lifted a single lotus flower into the air with his trunk, and prayed calmly. Instantly, help arrived to rescue him.', 'When things feel too heavy, stop fighting and ask for help.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Lifting the Earth to the Light', 'Puranas', [1], 'When the beautiful green planet fell deep into dark waters and was lost, a giant, gentle helper named Varaha dove deep down to save it. He carefully balanced the whole earth on his strong back and swam all the way up into the warm, bright sunlight, making it a safe and happy home once again.', 'You are always carried safely through the dark to the light.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('King Harishchandra’s Word', 'Puranas', [2], 'King Harishchandra made a promise to always speak the truth, no matter what happened. Even when he lost his grand palace, his wealth, and had to work hard in the fields, he never told a single lie or broke his word. Because his heart stayed clean and true, the universe rewarded him and gave him back everything tenfold.', 'Being honest keeps your heart clean and makes you truly strong.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Jatayu’s Brave Shield', 'Ramayana', [3], 'When an evil king tried to take Princess Sita away in his flying chariot, a brave old bird named Jatayu heard her calls for help. Even though he was old and did not have weapons, he flew straight into the sky and used his wings like a shield to block the path, fighting with all his might to keep her safe.', 'True bravery means standing up for others who need protection.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Steady Bowl of Oil', 'Puranas', [2], 'A teacher asked Narada to walk all the way around a loud, busy town while holding a bowl of water filled to the very brim, without spilling a single drop. Narada focused so deeply on keeping his hands steady that despite the noisy crowds and distractions, he didn\'t spill a drop and kept his mind perfectly calm.', 'You can find a quiet, still space even in a noisy world.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Shravan’s Balanced Journey', 'Ramayana', [3], 'Shravan Kumar loved his elderly parents deeply, but they were too tired to walk and could no longer see. To help them travel, he crafted two comfortable baskets, tied them to the ends of a strong bamboo stick, balanced the stick across his shoulders, and carried them happily on a long, smooth journey.', 'Love gives you the balance and strength to carry big duties.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Never-Ending Bowl of Food', 'Mahabharata', [1], 'A family living in the woods was given a magical copper bowl called the Akshaya Patra. This special bowl would create delicious, warm food automatically and would never run out, making sure that every guest, traveler, and child who visited their home went to sleep completely full, safe, and happy.', 'There is always enough love and care for everyone.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Little Upamanyu\'s Milk', 'Mahabharata', [1, 2], 'Little Upamanyu was a poor boy who loved milk, but his mother could only give him water mixed with white rice flour. Instead of crying, his mother told him to talk to the kind protector, Shiva. Upamanyu sat down under a tree, closed his eyes, and thought about Shiva with pure, sweet love. Because his wish was so simple and honest, Shiva blessed him with a whole ocean of fresh, sweet milk that never ran out.', 'When you ask with a pure and simple heart, the universe hears you.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('King Rantideva’s Kind Heart', 'Bhagavata Purana', [2], 'King Rantideva had no food or water for many days during a dry season. Finally, someone brought him a warm, delicious meal. Just as he sat down to eat, a hungry traveler knocked on his door. The king happily gave him half his food. Then, a poor man with hungry dogs arrived, and the king gave away the rest, staying hungry himself. He smiled warmly, happy that he could bring joy and comfort to others who needed it more.', 'Sharing what you have brings the sweetest joy to your heart.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Little Sage and the Ocean', 'Puranas', [3], 'Some big trouble-makers were hiding deep inside the vast ocean, making it hard for the good guys to find them. The gods asked a very small but wise teacher named Agastya for help. Everyone wondered how a little person could help with such a huge ocean. Agastya walked right up to the water, smiled, and drank up the entire ocean in one single, calm gulp, proving that your size doesn\'t limit how much good you can do.', 'Never underestimate yourself; big power can live in a small container.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('King Yudhishthira and His Dog', 'Mahabharata', [3], 'At the end of a long journey, King Yudhishthira reached the golden gates of heaven. A shining helper told him he could enter, but his loyal little dog, who had walked beside him through every difficult step, could not come inside. The king stopped and said, "If my faithful friend cannot enter, then I will stay outside with him." Because he showed such true love and loyalty, the gates opened wide for both of them.', 'Always stand by the friends who trust you and walk with you.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Wise Little Cobbler', 'Puranas', [2], 'A proud scholar and a simple cobbler were asked what they thought God could do. The scholar laughed and said it was impossible to do magical things. But the simple cobbler pointed to a tiny banyan tree seed and said, "If God can fit a massive, beautiful tree inside this tiny seed, He can do anything!" His simple, sweet faith showed everyone that true wisdom is seeing the magic in small things.', 'Simple faith and a happy heart see the beauty in everything.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Aruni’s Brave Day', 'Mahabharata', [3], 'A young boy named Aruni was looking after his teacher\'s farming field when a heavy rainstorm started breaking the muddy wall holding the water back. The water was rushing out fast. Aruni tried using sticks and mud, but the wall kept breaking. Seeing no other way, the brave boy lay down in the cold mud himself, using his own body to block the water until morning, saving the entire crop.', 'Being responsible means standing strong when others rely on you.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Karna’s Last Gift', 'Mahabharata', [2, 3], 'Karna was a famous warrior known for never saying "no" to anyone who asked for help. Even at the very end of a big battle, when he had nothing left, a poor man came to him asking for a gift. Karna realized he had one gold tooth left. Without hesitating, he broke the tooth and handed it to the traveler with a kind smile, keeping his promise to always be helpful.', 'Kindness is a treasure that stays in your heart forever.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Lakshmana’s Safe Line', 'Ramayana', [1, 2], 'Before leaving his sister-in-law Sita alone in their quiet forest cottage, Prince Lakshmana wanted to make sure she stayed completely safe. He took his bow and gently drew a simple line in the sand right in front of the door. He told her that as long as she stayed inside that safe line, no trouble or bad energy could ever touch her, creating a perfect shield of safety around her.', 'Safe boundaries protect you and keep you peaceful.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Devavrata’s Promise', 'Mahabharata', [3], 'Young Prince Devavrata loved his father very much. When he realized his father wanted to marry a kind fisherwoman, but her family was worried about the future, the prince stood up and made a great, unshakeable promise. He gave up his right to be king so his father could be perfectly happy, showing the world that family love is far more valuable than a golden crown.', 'Putting the happiness of your loved ones first makes you a true hero.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('King Janaka’s Calm Mind', 'Upanishads', [1, 2], 'King Janaka was sitting in a quiet room learning wise thoughts from a teacher when a messenger ran in screaming that the royal palace was on fire outside. While everyone else panicked and ran, the king sat perfectly still, his breath smooth and calm. He said, "My true inner peace cannot be burned by any fire." The fire turned out to be a magic trick by the teacher, who wanted to show everyone how steady the king’s heart truly was.', 'When you keep your mind calm, nothing outside can shake you.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Krishna’s Mouthful of Stars', 'Bhagavata Purana', [1], 'One day, little Krishna was playing in the dirt. His friends ran to his mother, Yashoda, and said, "Krishna is eating mud!" Yashoda ran out and told him to open his mouth. Krishna smiled and opened it wide. Instead of mud, his mother looked inside and saw the entire beautiful sky, the twinkling stars, the oceans, and all the mountains spinning gently. She realized her little boy was holding the whole wonderful world inside his sweet smile.', 'Great wonders can be hidden inside the smallest, most innocent things.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Prince Angada’s Steady Foot', 'Ramayana', [3], 'Prince Angada went to a big, noisy court full of strong soldiers to ask for peace. To prove the power of his team, he stepped forward, planted his right foot firmly on the stone floor, and made a challenge: "If anyone here can lift my foot even an inch off the ground, we win." The strongest warriors and giants tried with all their might, pulling and lifting, but Angada’s foot stayed glued to the ground like a mountain because his mind was completely steady.', 'When you stand firmly for what is right, nobody can shake your foundation.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Hanuman and the Healing Mountain', 'Ramayana', [3], 'During a difficult time, Rama’s brother needed a special herb that only grew on a faraway mountain. Hanuman flew across the sky to find it, but when he reached the mountain, he couldn\'t tell which plant was the right one because they all looked alike. Instead of wasting time or getting worried, Hanuman used his incredible strength to lift the entire mountain on his hand and flew it all the way back, saving everyone with his quick thinking.', 'If you can\'t find a small solution, think big and bring all your strength to the table.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('King Dilipa and the Safe Cow', 'Puranas', [2], 'King Dilipa was looking after a gentle sacred cow in the forest when a big lion jumped out to catch her. The king stepped right in front of the cow to block the lion. He said, "Take me instead, but do not hurt this gentle animal under my care." The lion smiled and turned into a bright light, revealing it was a test. Because the king was so brave and protective, he passed the test and was blessed with a beautiful, healthy family.', 'True courage means protecting those who are smaller or weaker than you.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Bhima and the Wise Old Monkey', 'Mahabharata', [2], 'Bhima was a very strong prince who thought nobody could beat him. While walking through the woods, he found an old, tired monkey blocking the path with his long tail. Bhima proudly said, "Move your tail, monkey!" The monkey replied, "I am too old and tired, please just lift it out of the way yourself." Bhima tried to lift the tail with one hand, then both hands, using all his mighty strength, but it wouldn\'t budge. The monkey then revealed he was actually the strong Hanuman, teaching Bhima to be humble.', 'Real strength doesn\'t mean being proud; true wisdom means respecting others.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Little Sparrow and the Big Ocean', 'Puranas', [2], 'A tiny sparrow laid her eggs on the beach, but a big wave swept them into the ocean. The sparrow didn\'t give up. She flew to the water, dipped her tiny beak in, and dropped the water on the sand, trying to dry up the ocean to get her eggs back. The giant eagle Garuda saw her tiny, endless effort and was so moved by her motherly love that he flew down and commanded the ocean to return her eggs safely.', 'No matter how small you feel, a mother\'s love can make the biggest things happen.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Little Boy Pipalada\'s Tree', 'Puranas', [1], 'A little baby boy named Pipalada was left near a giant Peepal tree. He had no house or parents to feed him, but the gentle tree looked after him, dropping sweet leaves for him to eat and providing cool shade from the hot sun. The boy grew up healthy, strong, and incredibly wise just by listening to the gentle rustling sound of the leaves, showing that nature is a wonderful protector.', 'Nature is always ready to feed, protect, and care for us if we trust it.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Krishna and the Sweet Butter Pot', 'Bhagavata Purana', [1], 'Little Krishna loved fresh, sweet butter more than anything. His mother would hide the butter pots high up near the ceiling so he couldn\'t reach them. Krishna simply gathered his little friends, had them stand on each other\'s shoulders to make a human ladder, climbed to the top, and shared the sweet butter with everyone, filling the whole house with laughter and sharing.', 'Working together with your loved ones makes every sweet victory even happier.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Shield over Uttara’s Baby', 'Mahabharata', [1, 2], 'A worried mother named Uttara was scared because a dangerous energy was heading toward her house while she was pregnant. She ran to Krishna and asked him to keep her unborn baby safe. Krishna smiled gently and created a bright, beautiful shield of light completely around her tummy. The dangerous energy bounced right off the shield without touching her, and the baby grew up safe, healthy, and happy.', 'You are always wrapped in a circle of safety and love that keeps you safe.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Rama and the Kind Boatman', 'Ramayana', [2], 'Rama needed to cross a wide, rushing river but had no boat. A simple boatman named Guha recognized Rama and offered his wooden boat happily. Before letting Rama step inside, Guha gently washed Rama\'s feet with clean water to show his love. Rama was so touched by the boatman\'s simple kindness that he hugged him tightly, treating him like a dear brother, showing that love breaks all barriers.', 'Simple kindness and true love can turn a stranger into family.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Bhagiratha’s Steady River', 'Puranas', [3], 'King Bhagiratha wanted to bring a beautiful, pure river down from the sky to help the dry earth. The river was so powerful that its fall could shake the ground. The king stayed perfectly focused and asked a wise protector to catch the crashing water safely. The river became a gentle, smooth, and steady stream that brought life and green trees to everyone.', 'When you stay focused and calm, big responsibilities become smooth and gentle.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Sudama\'s Humble Gift', 'Bhagavata Purana', [1], 'Sudama went to visit his old school friend, Krishna, who was now a great king living in a grand golden palace. Sudama was very poor and felt shy because he only brought a tiny cloth bundle of simple flattened rice as a gift. But Krishna was so happy to see his friend that he eagerly ate the rice with pure joy, secretly turning Sudama\'s broken little hut into a beautiful, happy home.', 'True love cares about the sweetness in your heart, not the cost of a gift.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Baby Krishna and the Two Trees', 'Bhagavata Purana', [1, 2], 'Little baby Krishna was tied to a heavy wooden rolling log by his mother so he wouldn\'t crawl away into trouble. Playful and strong, Krishna crawled anyway, pulling the heavy log right between two big, old trees that were stuck close together. With a gentle tug, he safely freed the trees and filled the whole garden with bright, happy energy.', 'Even when things feel heavy or stuck, love can gently set them free.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Lava and Kusha’s Beautiful Song', 'Ramayana', [2], 'Two twin boys named Lava and Kusha grew up in a quiet forest cottage. They learned to sing a beautiful, grand story with perfectly sweet voices and clear words. When they sang in front of a giant crowd, their voices were so gentle and tuneful that everyone stopped talking, closed their eyes, and felt a wave of absolute peace in their hearts.', 'Kind words and sweet music can bring peace to a whole room.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Ganesha’s Broken Tusk', 'Mahabharata', [2, 3], 'Ganesha sat down to write a very long and important book filled with wise lessons. While he was writing fast, his special pen suddenly snapped in half. Instead of stopping the work or getting upset, Ganesha quickly broke off a small piece of his own tusk, dipped it in ink, and kept writing without missing a single beat, showing everyone his great dedication.', 'When an obstacle comes your way, find a clever solution and keep going.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Three Giant Steps', 'Puranas', [2], 'A tiny boy named Vamana walked into a king\'s court and asked for just a small piece of land that he could cover in three simple steps. The king smiled and said yes. Suddenly, the little boy grew big and bright. With his first step, he covered the earth; with his second, he covered the sky; and for his third, the king happily offered his own heart, showing how big things can come from small beginnings.', 'Keep your promises and always think big, because you have great potential.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Sukanya’s Gift of Health', 'Puranas', [1, 2], 'Princess Sukanya lived in a quiet forest looking after an old, wise teacher who was very weak and could no longer see. She took care of him with so much love and gentle kindness every day that the divine helpers of health noticed. They blessed them with a special, sweet herbal juice that restored the old man’s eyesight and made him completely young, healthy, and strong again.', 'Gentle care and love are the best medicines for a healthy life.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Kind Palanquin Carrier', 'Bhagavata Purana', [2], 'A gentle man named Bharata was asked to help carry a king\'s royal chair along a dirt path. As he walked, Bharata kept gently jumping and shifting his steps to the side. The king asked why he was moving so unevenly. Bharata smiled kindly and pointed to the ground—he was shifting his weight to avoid stepping on a line of tiny little ants, protecting their fragile lives.', 'True strength is being gentle enough to protect even the smallest creatures.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Hardworking Farmer', 'Puranas', [1, 2], 'A simple farmer woke up early every day to plow his fields, look after his cows, and grow sweet corn. He was always happy. A wise traveler noticed that the farmer only said a small prayer of love in the morning when he woke up and at night before bed, yet he was the happiest man in the land because he did all his daily work with a joyful and loving heart.', 'Doing your daily duties with a happy smile is the most beautiful prayer.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Sita and the Golden Earth', 'Ramayana', [1], 'King Janaka was a kind leader who loved nature. One sunny morning, he was gently farming the dark, rich soil of his land when his plow touched something smooth. He dug carefully and discovered a beautiful golden box tucked safely in the earth. Inside was a happy, smiling baby girl named Sita. The king held her tight, realizing that new life is a precious, beautiful gift given to us by nature.', 'Every new child is a beautiful treasure waiting to be discovered.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Single Leaf of Love', 'Puranas', [1], 'Queen Satyabhama wanted to show how much she valued Krishna, so she decided to weigh him against gold and glittering jewels. She piled all her heavy gold coins on one side of a giant scale, but Krishna\'s side didn\'t move at all. She added more diamonds and silver, but the scale stayed down. Finally, a kind queen named Rukmini walked up and gently placed just one single green Tulsi leaf on the scale with pure love. Instantly, the scale balanced perfectly, showing that a tiny bit of true love weighs more than a mountain of gold.', 'Pure love and simple thoughts are worth more than any expensive things.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Hunter’s Pure Heart', 'Puranas', [2], 'A simple hunter named Thinnan lived in a deep forest and didn\'t know the proper rules or prayers. Every day, he brought fresh forest water in his mouth and simple wild flowers to put on a sacred stone under a tree. People thought he was doing it wrong, but the protector Shiva looked inside his heart and saw nothing but pure, unselfish love. Shiva blessed the hunter openly, showing everyone that the universe only cares about how much love you put into your actions.', 'It is the love inside your heart that makes your actions beautiful, not just doing things perfectly.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Moon\'s Humility Lesson', 'Shiva Purana', [2], 'One evening, little Ganesha was riding on his tiny friend, the mouse, after a happy feast. Suddenly, a small snake crossed their path, and the mouse jumped in fear, causing Ganesha to slip gently onto the grass. Up in the sky, the bright, beautiful moon saw this and laughed out loud with pride. Ganesha calmly looked up and reminded the moon that being bright shouldn\'t make you unkind to others. The moon felt sorry and hid its light, learning to grow softly and slowly every month with new sweetness and humility.', 'Always be kind and humble, even when you are shining bright.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Garuda\'s Great Flight', 'Mahabharata', [3], 'Garuda was a magnificent young bird whose mother was being treated unfairly by others. To set her free, he had to fly all the way up to a golden mountain and bring back a drop of special, sweet water that was guarded by big walls of flashing fire. Garuda didn\'t hesitate. He flew fast, swallowed water from a river to put out the fire walls, split open the barriers with his strong wings, and brought the sweet water home safely, freeing his mother with his brave and loving heart.', 'A child\'s love for their mother can give them the strength to overcome any hurdle.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Rushing River that Bowed', 'Bhagavata Purana', [1], 'On a dark, rainy night, a loving father named Vasudeva had to carry his newborn baby, little Krishna, across a wide and wild river to keep him safe. The rain was pouring down, and the river was rushing fast, rising higher and higher. But as the father stepped in, the gentle river water rose up just to softly touch the baby’s tiny foot. As soon as it felt the baby’s sweet energy, the river became completely calm, smooth, and quiet, lowering its waves to make a perfectly safe and dry path for them to cross.', 'When you take a step to protect love, the hardest paths open up smoothly for you.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Humble Little Feast', 'Puranas', [1, 2], 'A very wealthy being named Kubera hosted a massive feast to show off his golden plates and endless food. He invited little Ganesha, thinking he could impress him. Ganesha sat down and happily ate all the food in the palace, but he was still hungry. Kubera began to worry as his kitchens went empty. Finally, Shiva gave Kubera a tiny handful of simple roasted rice cooked with love. When Ganesha ate that one small, loving gift, he smiled, patted his tummy, and felt perfectly full and happy, teaching everyone that pride leaves you empty, but love fills you up.', 'Simple things given with true love bring the deepest happiness.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Pillar of Light', 'Bhagavata Purana', [2, 3], 'A proud king pointed to a stone pillar in his grand palace and mockingly asked his young son, Prahlada, "Is your protector inside this cold stone?" Prahlada smiled gently and replied, "He is everywhere, even in this pillar." Suddenly, the pillar split open with a bright light, and a powerful, loving protector named Narasimha stepped out to keep the boy safe from all harm, proving to the whole world that love and safety are always standing right beside you.', 'True protection is always around you, even in places you cannot see.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Single Golden Arrow', 'Shiva Purana', [3], 'Three giant flying cities made of gold, silver, and iron were causing a lot of noise and trouble across the sky. The warriors tried to stop them with thousands of weapons but failed. Finally, Shiva stepped forward. He didn\'t rush or get angry. He smiled calmly, drew back his bow string, and released just one single, perfectly aimed golden arrow. The arrow flew straight and true, gently dissolving all three troubled cities into beautiful white ash, restoring peace to the sky with absolute calmness.', 'A calm mind can solve big problems with just one simple, focused effort.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Brave Prince and the Fire Snake', 'Mahabharata', [2], 'Prince Nala was walking through a forest when he heard a tiny voice crying out for help from a ring of forest fire. He looked closely and saw a beautiful snake named Karkotaka trapped inside. Without any fear, Nala stepped through the smoke, picked up the little snake gently, and carried it out to a safe, cool green patch of grass. The snake thanked the prince and gave him a special gift that would shield and protect him from any hidden dangers or bad luck on his travels.', 'Helping someone who is scared always brings a shield of safety back to you.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Starry Sky Paradise', 'Ramayana', [2, 3], 'King Trishanku wanted to see the beautiful worlds above, but he couldn\'t fly. He asked a wise teacher named Vishwamitra for help. The teacher had promised to help the king, so he sat down, focused his mind, and used his creative thoughts to build a brand-new, magnificent paradise right in the middle of the sky, filled with glowing stars and peaceful paths just for the king, showing that a promise made out of love can create entirely new worlds.', 'When you keep your word with a clean heart, you can create wonderful new spaces for others.'),
];

const List<GarbhSacredStory> kGarbhGitaConversations = [
  GarbhSacredStory('The New Clothes', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 2, Verse 22', [1, 2], 'Arjuna felt worried about how things in life always change and grow old. Krishna smiled gently and said, "Look at your cloak, Arjuna. Just like you happily take off your old, dusty clothes at the end of the day to put on fresh, clean ones tomorrow, the beautiful life inside us never gets old. It simply steps into a wonderful new body to start a fresh journey."', 'Change is natural and is just the start of a beautiful new story.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Deep Ocean', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 2, Verse 70', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "How can a person stay steady when life brings so many shifting feelings?" Krishna pointed toward the sea and said, "Look at the great ocean, Arjuna. Countless rushing rivers constantly pour into it with loud splashes, trying to shake it up. But the ocean stays perfectly calm, deep, and steady, absorbing them all without overflowing. Be like the ocean—let worries melt into your deep peace."', 'Keep your inner heart deep and calm, no matter how noisy the world gets.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Leaf and the Flower', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 9, Verse 26', [1], 'Arjuna wondered if he needed grand, expensive gifts to show his love to the universe. Krishna shook his head, picked up a tiny green leaf from the ground, and said, "I do not need grand treasures. If someone offers me just a single leaf, a little flower, a sweet piece of fruit, or a single drop of clean water with a happy, loving heart, I accept it with absolute joy. It is the love that matters."', 'The simplest things are the most precious when given with pure love.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Still Flame', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 6, Verse 19', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "What does a calm and beautifully focused mind look like?" Krishna answered, "Think of a little candle flame sitting inside a quiet room where there is no wind blowing. Because there are no outside gusts of air to shake it, the flame stands perfectly straight, steady, and bright. When you focus on quiet, happy thoughts, your mind becomes just like that beautiful, still flame."', 'A quiet mind stands straight and steady without flickering.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Beautiful Tree', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 15, Verse 1', [3], 'Arjuna looked at a tree and asked where we get our true strength from. Krishna shared a beautiful secret: "Think of a sacred tree whose roots reach all the way up into the peaceful sky, while its branches and leaves grow down to touch our daily world. This reminds us that our true inner strength and life force always come from a high, peaceful, and loving place above us."', 'Your real strength comes from a deep, peaceful place inside you.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Wise Turtle', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 2, Verse 58', [2, 3], 'Arjuna looked at the busy crowd and asked, "How do I protect my peace when everything around me is rushing?" Krishna said, "Think of a wise turtle, Arjuna. Whenever it feels too much noise or trouble around it, it simply draws its limbs inside its strong, safe shell to rest in quiet safety. You can do the same—whenever worries rush in, just draw your thoughts inward to your own quiet center."', 'You can always pull your thoughts inside to find a quiet, safe space.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Calming the Wind', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 6, Verses 34-35', [2], 'Arjuna sighed and said, "Krishna, my mind is running around so fast! Trying to stop my thoughts feels as hard as trying to catch the blowing wind." Krishna answered gently, "You are right, my friend, the mind is restless and hard to catch. But do not get upset with it. With patient, daily practice and by taking calm, deep breaths, you can guide your thoughts to sit quietly right beside you."', 'With patience and gentle breaths, you can calm any busy thought.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Dusty Mirror', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 3, Verse 38', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Why do we sometimes feel confused or lose our inner peace?" Krishna pointed to a mirror and said, "Just like a layer of dust can make a clean mirror look blurry, or smoke can hide a bright fire, feelings of worry or anger can hide the beautiful wisdom inside your heart. Just take a deep breath, clear away the worry, and your inner light will shine clearly again."', 'Wiping away worry reveals the beautiful, bright peace already inside you.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Bright Sun', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 13, Verse 33', [1], 'Arjuna asked, "How can one small soul bring life to this whole big body?" Krishna pointed out at the morning sky and said, "Look at the sun, Arjuna. It sits high up in one single spot in space, yet its warm, bright light reaches down to touch, wake up, and warm the entire world. In the exact same way, the beautiful spark of life inside you warms and brightens every single cell."', 'One tiny spark of life fills your whole body with warmth and energy.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Safe Spark', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 2, Verses 23-24', [1, 2], 'Arjuna was worried that difficult times might hurt who he was on the inside. Krishna touched his shoulder and said, "Listen to this beautiful secret, Arjuna: no sharp weapon can ever cut your true inner soul, no hot fire can burn it, no rushing water can make it wet, and no dry wind can ever sweep it away. You are completely solid, safe, and unbreakable on the inside."', 'Who you are on the inside is always safe, strong, and protected.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Changing Seasons', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 2, Verse 14', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "How do I handle days that feel too hot or days that feel too cold and heavy?" Krishna smiled and said, "Think of the winter and the summer seasons, Arjuna. They come, stay for a little while, and then they always pass away to let the next season come. Feelings of joy and sadness are just like that—they come and go like the wind. Just watch them pass, knowing you are steady."', 'Difficult days and happy days come and go like the changing seasons.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Circle of Safety', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 4, Verse 8', [1], 'Arjuna asked, "Does the universe look after us when things feel chaotic?" Krishna held his hand and promised, "Whenever goodness is weak and things feel upside down, I manifest myself to protect the kind, clear the path of trouble, and restore sweet balance. You never have to fear, because a great shield of love is always looking after you."', 'You are always guarded and protected by a great shield of love.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Your Best Friend', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 6, Verse 5', [2], 'Arjuna sat under a tree, feeling tired of his own negative thoughts. Krishna sat beside him and said, "Your own mind can be a troublemaker, or it can be your very best friend. When you choose gentle thoughts and listen to calm stories, you train your mind to hold your hand like a loyal best friend who always helps you feel brave and happy."', 'Be kind to your thoughts, and your mind will become your best friend.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Seated in the Heart', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 10, Verse 20', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, where can I find you when I feel lonely?" Krishna placed a warm hand directly over Arjuna\'s chest and said, "I am not faraway in the clouds, my friend. I am seated right here, inside the very heart of every living creature. I am there at the beginning, I am there in the middle, and I am there forever. You are never, ever alone."', 'The divine spirit lives right inside your heart, so you are never alone.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Rest and Let Go', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 18, Verse 61', [3], 'Arjuna felt exhausted from trying to control everything around him. Krishna looked at him with great affection and said, "The loving protector lives inside the heart of everyone, guiding this whole world like a beautiful, gentle machine. Let go of trying to fix every little thing, Arjuna. Take a deep breath, relax your shoulders, and let the universe carry you safely."', 'Let go of what you cannot control and rest in perfect safety.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Enjoy the Journey', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 2, Verse 47', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "How do I work without stressing over what will happen in the future?" Krishna answered, "Your only job is to focus completely on doing your best right now with a happy smile. Do not spend your energy worrying about the rewards or what comes next. Enjoy the step you are taking right now, and the results will blossom beautifully on their own."', 'Focus on doing your work with joy, and don\'t worry about what comes next.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Staying Steady', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 12, Verse 15', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "Who is a person that brings true joy to the world?" Krishna replied, "The one who does not get frightened or agitated by the noisy world, and the one who never makes others feel scared or upset either. A person who stays free from hurry, fear, and anger is very dear to the universe and carries a beautiful, quiet strength."', 'A gentle heart brings peace to itself and everyone around it.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('No More Worries', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 18, Verse 66', [3], 'Arjuna felt overwhelmed by all the rules and duties he had to balance. Krishna looked at him with absolute love and said, "Leave all your endless worries and heavy fears behind, Arjuna. Just come to me and rest in my love alone. I will shield you from every single trouble and make your heart completely free. Do not worry at all."', 'When you share your burdens with love, fear completely disappears.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Pure and Happy Food', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 17, Verse 8', [1], 'Arjuna asked, "What kind of things should we bring into our body to feel good?" Krishna explained, "The foods that give us long life, strength, health, and clean happiness are foods that are sweet, juicy, fresh, and natural. Eating simple, wholesome things makes your body strong, your mind calm, and fills your whole house with a happy energy."', 'Choosing fresh and natural things makes your body and mind feel happy.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Bright Spark of Life', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 10, Verse 41', [1, 2], 'Arjuna looked out at the beautiful world and asked, "Where does all the beauty and power in nature come from?" Krishna answered, "Whenever you see something full of life, something beautiful, something strong, or something glowing with joy, know that it is born from just a tiny, single spark of my bright light."', 'Every beautiful and joyful thing is a small spark of a grand, loving light.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Lotus Leaf', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 5, Verse 10', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, how can I live in a world full of messy problems without letting them make me feel sad or muddy?" Krishna pointed to a pond and said, "Look at the beautiful lotus flower, Arjuna. It grows right out of the muddy water, but its large green leaves stay completely clean and dry because the water slides right off them. Live like the lotus leaf—let worldly worries slide right off you, staying pure and untouched."', 'You can live in a busy world but still stay completely pure and clean inside.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Little Wandering Puppy', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 6, Verse 26', [2], 'Arjuna confessed, "Krishna, even when I sit down to rest, my mind just wanders away to a hundred different places!" Krishna smiled warmly and said, "Whenever your restless mind slips away, Arjuna, do not pull it back angrily. Just treat it like a sweet little puppy that has trotted off. Gently lift it up with love and place it back into your quiet heart, over and over, until it feels safe enough to stay."', 'Gently bring your thoughts back to peace whenever they wander away.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Two Hands of Protection', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 9, Verse 22', [1], 'Arjuna asked, "What happens to someone who relies completely on the love of the universe?" Krishna held up both his hands and promised, "For those who think of me with an open heart and stay connected to love, I take full responsibility for them. I personally carry what they lack, and I safely guard everything they already have. They are always completely taken care of."', 'When you trust the universe, you are always completely provided for and safe.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('One Big Family', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 18, Verse 20', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, what is the highest kind of wisdom a person can have?" Krishna looked out at the birds, the trees, and the people passing by and said, "The highest wisdom is the eye that looks at everything in the universe and sees that we are all made of the exact same beautiful light. Even though everyone looks different on the outside, we are all part of one single, loving family on the inside."', 'Real wisdom is seeing the same beautiful light inside every living creature.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Smooth Walking Path', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 2, Verse 48', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "How do I walk through life without stumbling over unexpected surprises?" Krishna answered, "Walk with an even mind, Arjuna. Do not get wildly excited when things go perfectly right, and do not get deeply upset when things go unexpectedly wrong. When you stay balanced and smooth through both the ups and downs, your path becomes effortless and happy."', 'Staying balanced through the ups and downs makes your life smooth and happy.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Lamp in the Dark', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 10, Verse 11', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "How do you help us when our hearts feel heavy or confused?" Krishna answered gently, "Out of pure love for you, Arjuna, I stand right inside your heart. I pick up a bright, glowing lamp made of pure wisdom and shine its warm light all around. That light instantly melts away all the dark shadows of confusion and doubt, leaving your mind clean and bright."', 'The light of love inside you can instantly chase away any dark worry.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Same Heartbeat', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 6, Verse 29', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "How does a happy person treat others?" Krishna said, "A truly peaceful person sees themselves in everyone else, Arjuna. When they see someone else smiling, they feel happy too. When they see someone else hurting, they gently step in to help, because they know that we all share the same heartbeat and the same spark of life."', 'Treating others with love is the same as being loving to yourself.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Soft and Quiet Voice', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 17, Verse 16', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "What is the best way to use my mind and my words every day?" Krishna whispered softly, "Keep your mind gentle and pleasant, Arjuna. Choose words that are completely true, sweet to hear, and kind to others. When you practice beautiful silence and keep your thoughts clean and honest, your whole body fills up with a comforting, healthy energy."', 'Kind words and quiet thoughts create a beautiful, healthy home inside you.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Steady Mountain Lake', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 2, Verse 56', [3], 'Arjuna asked, "What is the secret of a person who is truly strong?" Krishna said, "Think of a quiet mountain lake, Arjuna. Even when big stones drop into it, its water stays clear. A strong person is someone whose heart is free from wild anger, free from constant wanting, and free from fear. Because they are anchored in love, their peace stays as solid as a mountain."', 'True strength means staying calm and free from fear and anger.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Unchanging Guide', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 18, Verse 73', [3], 'At the very end of their long talk, Arjuna took a deep breath, smiled with great relief, and said, "Krishna, all my doubts are completely gone now. My mind is perfectly still, my heart feels incredibly brave, and I am ready to walk forward because I remember who I truly am." Krishna nodded with absolute love, knowing his friend was safe.', 'Remembering that you are loved makes you brave enough for any journey.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Jewels on a Thread', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 7, Verse 7', [1, 2], 'Arjuna looked up at the stars and asked, "Krishna, what holds this beautiful world together so perfectly?" Krishna smiled and said, "Look at a beautiful necklace, Arjuna. You see the bright, sparkling gems, but you don\'t see the thread inside. I am like that invisible, gentle thread, holding all of life together in one safe, loving design."', 'We are all beautifully connected by a gentle thread of love.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Flute and the Music', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 11, Verse 33', [2, 3], 'Arjuna felt small and worried, asking, "How can I do big, brave things when I feel so tired?" Krishna touched his hand and whispered, "Think of a simple wooden flute, Arjuna. On its own, it is just a quiet piece of wood. But when it allows the musician to breathe through it, it plays the most beautiful songs. Just relax, be like that gentle flute, and let the universe bring out your inner music."', 'Relax and trust that you have all the strength you need inside you.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Fire and the Smoke', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 18, Verse 48', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, why is it so hard to make everything in life completely perfect?" Krishna pointed to a warm campfire and said, "Look at the cozy fire, Arjuna. It gives us warm light and cooks our food, but it always has a little bit of smoke around it too. Nothing in this world is completely perfect. Do not hate the warm fire just because of a little smoke—focus on the warmth and let the smoke drift away."', 'Focus on the good things in life and let the little flaws go.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The House with Bright Windows', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 14, Verse 11', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "How can I tell when my heart is full of true goodness and peace?" Krishna answered, "Think of a cozy little house at night, Arjuna. When the house is full of light inside, every single window shines brightly out into the dark. When your heart is full of happy, kind thoughts, your eyes, your smile, and your whole body will naturally shine with a warm, gentle light."', 'When you choose happy thoughts, your whole body shines with peace.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Gentle Step-by-Step', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 6, Verse 25', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, how do I calm my mind down when it feels completely overwhelmed?" Krishna answered softly, "Do it gently, my friend, like walking down a safe flight of stairs. You don\'t jump all the way to the bottom. Step by step, using your clever mind to think good thoughts, quietly lead your heart back to a safe, restful space until it settles down beautifully."', 'Be patient and gentle with yourself, taking one small step at a time.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Sweetest Honey', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 4, Verse 38', [1], 'Arjuna asked, "What is the cleanest, most beautiful thing we can find in this world?" Krishna looked at him with great love and said, "There is nothing in this whole world as pure and sweet as inner wisdom, Arjuna. When you live a kind life, this sweet knowledge washes over your heart like a pure, clean river, making you feel completely happy and refreshed inside."', 'Good wisdom keeps your heart clean, fresh, and happy.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Warm Rain Cloud', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 9, Verse 19', [2, 3], 'Arjuna looked out at a dry field and asked, "Where does the energy of life come from?" Krishna answered, "I am the warm sunshine that wakes up the sleeping flowers, Arjuna. And when the earth gets thirsty, I become the fluffy gray cloud that showers sweet, cool rain to make the grass turn bright green. The universe is always sending you exactly what you need to grow."', 'The universe is always looking after you, giving you what you need.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Unshakeable Anchor', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 6, Verse 22', [3], 'Arjuna asked, "What does true, deep happiness feel like?" Krishna smiled and said, "It is a joy so big and deep, Arjuna, that once you hold it in your heart, no other prize looks bigger. It is like an anchor that holds a ship so steady that even if a massive storm with heavy waves crashes against it, the ship stays perfectly safe and never sinks."', 'True inner peace is a shield that stands strong against any worry.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Mirror in the Stream', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 14, Verse 17', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "What happens when we fill our days with quiet, calm actions?" Krishna pointed to a clear, still mountain stream and said, "When the water is perfectly still, you can see your own happy reflection clearly, and the birds can drink safely. Doing quiet, gentle things gives you a clear mind and a happy heart, making you a safe place for everyone around you."', 'A quiet and gentle life brings clarity and happiness to everyone.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Open Doorway', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 5, Verse 19', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "Who can overcome the difficulties of this changing world right now?" Krishna held his hand and said, "The ones whose minds are perfectly steady and equal to everyone, Arjuna. When you treat the rich and the poor, the small and the large with the exact same loving smile, your heart matches the pure, flawless nature of the universe, and you are already living in paradise."', 'Treating everyone with the same kindness makes your world beautiful.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Gentle Words', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 17, Verse 15', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, how should I speak so my words bring peace?" Krishna replied, "Speak words that do not agitate others, words that are completely honest, sweet to hear, and full of helpful truth. When you speak kindly, your voice becomes a gentle medicine that calms everyone around you."', 'Kind and honest words bring comfort to everyone.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Seed of Trust', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 4, Verse 39', [1], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, who is the one who finds the deepest wisdom and peace?" Krishna held his hand and said, "The one who has deep trust and keeps their mind focused, Arjuna. When you have trust in the goodness of the universe, all your doubts melt away, and a beautiful, quiet peace wraps around your heart like a warm blanket."', 'Trusting the goodness around you brings deep inner peace.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Quiet Observer', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 14, Verses 22-23', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "How do I stay calm when my thoughts switch between being super active and feeling completely lazy?" Krishna smiled and said, "Just sit back and watch them like a quiet observer, Arjuna. Do not run after the busy thoughts, and do not get upset when you feel slow. Let those moods come and go like clouds in the sky, while you stay completely still and undisturbed underneath."', 'You are not your changing moods; you are the calm space underneath them.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Playing Your Part', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 18, Verse 46', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, do I have to do extraordinary things to make the universe happy?" Krishna shook his head and said, "Not at all, my friend. The great power that created this entire world is right here. When you simply do your daily tasks with a happy heart and a loving smile, you are turning your ordinary day into a beautiful prayer."', 'Doing your daily activities with love is the highest form of prayer.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Constant Song', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 10, Verse 25', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, out of all the ways to connect with you, which one is the sweetest?" Krishna whispered, "The sweetest way is Japa—silently repeating a calm, beautiful name or thought inside your mind. It requires no heavy lifting, just a gentle, constant song of love inside your heart that keeps you feeling safe and happy all day long."', 'Keeping a sweet, happy thought in your heart keeps you peaceful all day.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Golden Eye', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 13, Verse 28', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "What is the secret to never hurting myself or others?" Krishna answered, "Look at the world with a golden eye, Arjuna. See that the exact same loving protector lives inside every person and every little creature. When you see that everyone shares the same life force, you will naturally treat everyone with gentle kindness, and your own path will become beautiful."', 'Seeing the same light in everyone fills your own heart with kindness.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Rising Bird', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 2, Verse 45', [3], 'Arjuna asked, "How do I deal with the world when it keeps pulling me between wanting things and fearing loss?" Krishna said, "Rise above those pairs of opposites, Arjuna. Be like a bird that flies high above the ground. Let go of the constant worry of saving this or wanting that. Just anchor yourself in your true, quiet self, where you are already rich and perfectly safe."', 'True safety comes from resting in who you are, not from what you own.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Gentle Friend', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 12, Verse 13', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, tell me about the traits of someone who is deeply loved by the universe." Krishna smiled and said, "It is the one who is a kind friend to every living creature, Arjuna. They do not hold grudges, they do not think \'this is mine,\' and they are full of soft compassion. They treat joy and sadness with the same calm smile, carrying a gentle heart wherever they go."', 'A gentle and compassionate heart is the greatest treasure in the world.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Resting Place', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 18, Verse 65', [3], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, what is your ultimate promise to me when I feel lost?" Krishna looked at him with absolute, overflowing love and said, "Give me your mind, fill your heart with my love, and rest your thoughts in me. I give you my true, unshakeable promise: you will come straight to me and live in my joyful light forever, because you are incredibly dear to me."', 'You are deeply loved by the universe, and you always have a safe home.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Precious Gem', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 7, Verse 3', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Is it easy to find this beautiful path of inner peace?" Krishna answered gently, "Out of many people, only a few truly stop to look for this quiet path, Arjuna. And out of those who look, only a few truly realize how beautiful it is. You are here, listening to these quiet truths, which means your heart is already a rare and precious gem."', 'Valuing peace and quiet wisdom makes your heart rare and beautiful.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Scattered Tree Branches', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 2, Verse 41', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, why does my mind feel so tired when I have too many things to think about?" Krishna answered, "When a person is worried, their thoughts are like a tree with thousands of scattered branches going in every direction, getting tangled up. But when your mind is calm and clear, your thoughts follow just one single, beautiful path that leads straight to peace."', 'A calm mind follows one clear, happy path instead of getting tangled up.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Middle String', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 6, Verse 16', [1], 'Arjuna asked, "How do I keep my body and my mind feeling perfectly happy and healthy every day?" Krishna smiled and said, "It is all about balance, my friend. A person cannot find true peace if they eat too much or if they do not eat enough. They cannot find rest if they sleep all day or if they do not sleep enough. Always find the happy middle path, and your body will feel wonderful."', 'Finding the happy middle balance keeps your body and mind healthy.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Bitter Medicine', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 18, Verse 37', [3], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, why does doing the right thing or sitting quietly sometimes feel a little hard at first?" Krishna explained gently, "True and lasting happiness is like a special medicine, Arjuna. It might taste a little bitter or feel a little difficult when you first try it, but in the end, it turns into the sweetest nectar that fills your whole life with joy."', 'Good things might feel a little hard at first, but they bring the sweetest rewards.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Single Lamp', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 13, Verse 16', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, how can the divine spirit live inside every single person at the same time without being split into pieces?" Krishna pointed to a small light and said, "Think of a single lamp, Arjuna. It can light up a hundred different candles all over the room. Each candle shines brightly on its own, but the main light stays whole and undivided. That is how love lives inside everyone at once."', 'The same whole light of love lives inside every single one of us.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Gift of Pure Sunshine', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 14, Verse 6', [1], 'Arjuna asked, "What does it feel like when our heart is filled with pure goodness and light?" Krishna answered happily, "It feels just like warm, clear sunshine inside your chest, Arjuna. It is perfectly clean and healthy. It chases away all dark worries, makes you want to smile, fills you with a desire to learn new things, and makes your heart feel completely light."', 'Pure goodness feels like warm sunshine that washes away all worries.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Hidden Seed', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 10, Verse 39', [1], 'Arjuna looked out at the vast green valley and asked, "Where does the magic of life begin, Krishna?" Krishna whispered softly, "There is no breathing creature, no tall tree, no little bird, and no tiny baby that can exist without me, Arjuna. I am the hidden seed of life inside everything. Every single living thing grows from this same beautiful spark."', 'Every living thing grows from the same magical seed of life.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Choosing the Happy Road', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 9, Verse 31', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "What happens if a person has a bad day or makes a big mistake? Are they lost forever?" Krishna shook his head with absolute love and said, "Never, Arjuna. The very moment a person stops, changes their mind, and chooses a kind, peaceful road, they instantly become good. Their heart changes, and they find a quiet safety that never disappears."', 'It is never too late to choose a kind, gentle, and happy path.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Big Picture', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 18, Verse 22', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "Why do some people get so angry over little things?" Krishna answered, "Because they have a narrow view, Arjuna. They look at just one tiny thing and think it is the whole world, ignoring everything else. Open your eyes wide, look at the big picture, and see how vast and beautiful the whole universe truly is."', 'Look at the big, beautiful picture instead of worrying over tiny things.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Washing the Bowl', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 5, Verse 11', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Why should we practice doing good things quietly without telling everyone about it?" Krishna said, "Think of washing a small glass bowl until it is clean, shiny, and bright. We don\'t do it to show off to the neighbors; we do it simply because a clean bowl is a joy to hold. Do kind things quietly just to keep your own heart clean and shiny."', 'Do kind things quietly simply to keep your own heart clean and bright.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Steady Rock', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 6, Verse 7', [3], 'Arjuna asked, "How should I react when people say nice things or when they say mean things?" Krishna pointed to a large stone and said, "Be like a steady rock in the meadow, Arjuna. When the cold rain falls on it, it stays steady. When the warm sun shines on it, it stays exactly the same. Keep your inner heart calm and steady, whether things around you feel cold or warm."', 'Stay calm and steady on the inside, no matter what happens on the outside.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Sweetness of Water', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 7, Verse 8', [1, 2], 'Arjuna took a sip of cool river water and asked, "Krishna, where can I feel your presence in my everyday life?" Krishna smiled and said, "I am the crisp, sweet taste of fresh water when you are thirsty, Arjuna. I am the bright morning light of the sun and the moon, and I am the soft, beautiful sound echoing through the quiet air."', 'The beauty and goodness in nature are signs of a loving universe.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Full Fountain', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 2, Verse 46', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "When someone finds this big inner peace, do they still need to chase after small pleasures?" Krishna pointed to a wide, clear lake and said, "When you have a massive, deep lake filled with sweet, fresh water right in front of you, you no longer need to look for a tiny little puddle. Finding your inner joy satisfies your heart completely."', 'True happiness inside makes you feel completely full and content.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Quiet Joy', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 6, Verses 20-21', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "What happens when our thoughts become perfectly quiet?" Krishna replied, "When the mind rests in quiet stillness, it becomes completely satisfied from within. You feel a deep, beautiful joy that is far sweeter than anything you can touch or see with your outer senses, and your heart never wants to leave that peaceful space."', 'True peace brings a quiet joy that satisfies your whole heart.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Sharing Everything', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 9, Verse 27', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "How do I stay close to your love while I am busy doing my daily chores?" Krishna answered gently, "Whatever you do, whatever you eat, whatever sweet gift you give to others, and even when you take a moment to rest—just offer it all to me with a happy heart. When you share your day with love, everything you do becomes peaceful."', 'Sharing your daily actions with love fills your day with peace.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Think It Over Freely', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 18, Verse 63', [2], 'Arjuna listened closely and asked, "Must I follow this path exactly as you say?" Krishna looked at him with great respect and said, "I have shared the deepest, most beautiful secrets of life with you, my friend. Now, take your time, think it over calmly in your heart, and then choose exactly what you want to do with full freedom."', 'The universe gives you the freedom to choose your own happy path.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Cozy Nest of Goodness', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 14, Verse 18', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "Where do our daily choices take us, Krishna?" Krishna answered, "When you choose actions that are kind, calm, and good, your mind naturally rises into a bright, happy place. When you live with hurry and anger, you stay stuck in worry. Always choose the path of gentle goodness, and you will live in a cozy nest of peace."', 'Choosing kind and gentle actions lifts your heart to a happy place.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Clear the Shadows', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 4, Verse 42', [3], 'Arjuna felt a little confused about his duties. Krishna stepped close, handed him his bow, and said, "The doubts in your mind are just dark shadows born out of not knowing the truth, Arjuna. Use the sharp sword of inner wisdom to cut those doubts away. Stand up tall, take a deep breath, and walk forward with a brave heart."', 'Wisdom chases away doubt, making you feel strong and brave.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Happy Little Child', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 2, Verse 55', [1], 'Arjuna asked, "How does a deeply peaceful person behave on the inside?" Krishna explained, "A peaceful person is like a happy little child who doesn\'t need external toys to smile. They let go of constant selfish cravings and find absolute joy simply by resting in their own kind, loving heart. They are perfectly content just being who they are."', 'Real happiness comes from loving who you are on the inside.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Voice Inside', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 15, Verse 15', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "Where do our good ideas and memories come from when we need them?" Krishna smiled and whispered, "I am seated deep inside the heart of everyone, Arjuna. From me comes the quiet wisdom to make good choices, the clear memory to remember love, and the peaceful strength to let go of old worries."', 'Your inner heart always holds the wisdom and memory you need.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Team of Victory', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 18, Verse 78', [3], 'At the very end of the battlefield, the wise observer Sanjaya said, "Wherever there is the wise protector Krishna sharing love, and wherever there is the brave student Arjuna listening with a clear mind, there will always be bright victory, sweet prosperity, endless joy, and perfect balance."', 'When love and focus work together, happiness always wins.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Radiant Sun', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 10, Verse 21', [1, 2], 'Arjuna looked up at the sky and asked, "Krishna, if I want to see your bright energy in nature, where should I look?" Krishna laughed happily and said, "Among all the glowing lights in the universe, Arjuna, I am the radiant morning sun that wakes up the world. Among all the stars at night, I am the soft, beautiful moon. Look at them and feel my warm presence."', 'You are connected to the brightest, most beautiful lights in the universe.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Contented Heart', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 12, Verse 14', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, how does a person behave when they are completely happy with themselves?" Krishna answered, "They are always content with whatever they have, Arjuna. They keep their mind and body under gentle control, their convictions are strong and steady, and they have given their whole heart to love. A person like that is incredibly dear to me."', 'True happiness comes from being content with who you are and what you have.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Seven Sweet Blessings', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 10, Verse 34', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "What are the most beautiful qualities that bring grace to our world?" Krishna smiled and said, "Listen closely, Arjuna. I live inside the highest virtues of life: inside good fame, sweet fortune, kind and gentle speech, clear memory, clever intelligence, unshakeable steadfastness, and patient forgiveness. When you practice these, you are sharing my light."', 'Kindness, patience, and clear speech make your life completely beautiful.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Equal Eye', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 5, Verse 18', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, how does a truly wise person look at the world?" Krishna answered, "A wise person looks at a learned teacher, a big gentle cow, a mighty elephant, and a little playful dog with the exact same loving eye, Arjuna. They do not see differences on the outside; they only see the same beautiful spark of life inside everyone."', 'True wisdom means treating every living thing with the exact same kind love.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Quiet Strength', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 13, Verse 7', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "What is the truest sign that someone is growing wiser?" Krishna answered softly, "It is when they are completely humble, Arjuna. They do not brag or show off, they never try to hurt anyone, they are full of soft patience, they are simple and honest, and they treat their loved ones and teachers with deep, genuine respect."', 'Being humble and gentle makes you far stronger than being proud.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Brave Spark', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 16, Verse 1', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "What is the very first step to living a glorious and happy life?" Krishna stood tall and said, "It is complete fearlessness, Arjuna. When your heart is pure, when you stand steadily by your inner wisdom, when you are generous and keep your senses calm, fear can never find a home inside you."', 'When your heart is clean and pure, you can walk through life completely without fear.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('What You Believe, You Become', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 17, Verse 3', [1], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, why do people look and act so differently from one another?" Krishna explained gently, "Everyone carries a specific kind of faith inside their heart, Arjuna. A person is completely made of their own beliefs. Whatever you choose to believe in with your whole heart, that is exactly what you turn into."', 'Choose to believe in beautiful, happy, and loving things, because you become what you think.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Clean and Untroubled Mind', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 12, Verse 16', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, who can live in this world without getting stressed out?" Krishna answered, "The one who is completely pure on the inside, expert at what they do, yet completely free from anxiety, Arjuna. They don\'t take sides, they don\'t worry about outcomes, and they stay peaceful no matter what happens around them."', 'Stay pure, do your best, and let go of all unnecessary worries.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Great Promise of Balance', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 4, Verse 7', [3], 'Arjuna looked at the changing world and asked, "What happens when goodness disappears from the earth?" Krishna held his hand tightly and promised, "Whenever goodness grows weak and things become chaotic, Arjuna, I personally step forward to bring back light, clear away the trouble, and restore sweet balance to the world."', 'The universe will always bring back balance and look after you when things get tough.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Welcoming Every Single Day', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 18, Verse 54', [3], 'Arjuna asked, "What is the final state of a person who has found your light?" Krishna smiled warmly and said, "Their mind becomes perfectly serene, Arjuna. They never grieve over what is gone, and they never anxiously crave what is missing. They welcome every single day with joy and see all living beings with the exact same loving smile."', 'True peace means living happily in the present moment, loving everyone just as they are.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Light in the Sky', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 15, Verse 12', [1, 2], 'Arjuna looked at the morning horizon and asked, "Krishna, where does the wonderful glow of the day come from?" Krishna answered softly, "The warm light that brightens the great sun, the soft silver glow that wakes up the moon at night, and the cozy heat of the campfire—all of that beautiful light comes straight from my loving heart to warm the world."', 'Every bright light in nature is a small reminder of a big love.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Voice of Wisdom', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 10, Verse 10', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, when I am confused, how do I know the right path to take?" Krishna touched his heart and said, "For those who stay close to me with love, I step inside their minds and give them a gentle inner voice. This quiet voice whispers the exact wisdom they need, guiding their steps safely down the happiest path."', 'Listen to your quiet inner guide; it always knows the way to love.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Rested Traveler', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 5, Verse 12', [3], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, why do some people walk through life so lightly, without any fatigue?" Krishna explained warmly, "Because they are like rested travelers, Arjuna. They do their daily tasks with love, but they do not carry the heavy weight of worrying about what will happen tomorrow. They leave the future to the universe and walk with a free heart."', 'Letting go of tomorrow’s worries helps you walk lightly today.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Cool Summer Day', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 12, Verse 18', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "How can I stay perfectly peaceful when people are unkind or judge me?" Krishna said, "Be like a cool summer breeze, Arjuna. Treat praise and criticism, heat and cold, friends and unkind people with the exact same soft smile. Your inner happiness does not have to change just because the weather outside changes."', 'Your inner heart can stay sunny and warm, no matter how cold the world gets.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Rhythmic Dance', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 6, Verse 17', [1], 'Arjuna asked, "How do I make my everyday life feel sweet and healthy?" Krishna smiled and said, "Think of life like a beautiful, rhythmic dance, Arjuna. Eat foods that give you strength, take a gentle walk, do your work happily, and get plenty of deep sleep on time. When your daily rhythm is balanced, all your physical pains gently melt away."', 'A balanced daily routine keeps your body and mind feeling joyful.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Clean Slate', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 9, Verse 30', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "What if a person has been angry or made mistakes in the past? Can they ever fix it?" Krishna shook his head with great comfort and said, "The very moment someone turns around and chooses love, kindness, and peace, their past vanishes. They have wiped their slate completely clean, and they are already a beautiful, good person."', 'You can always choose to start fresh with a kind and gentle heart.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Blooming Garden', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 10, Verse 35', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "What part of the changing year feels most like your presence, Krishna?" Krishna smiled brightly and said, "Among all the lovely seasons of the earth, I am the blooming springtime. I am the time when the flowers open up their petals, the birds sing sweet songs, and the whole world fills up with fresh life and bright color."', 'New beginnings are full of natural beauty, joy, and fresh life.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Happy Skies', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 11, Verse 36', [3], 'Arjuna looked up at the vast sky and asked, "What happens when love wins over trouble?" Krishna answered with absolute joy, "The whole universe rejoices, Arjuna! The stars dance, the fields sing, and all the dark shadows of fear run away because the bright light of love has filled the room, making everyone completely safe."', 'Love makes the whole world feel happy, safe, and full of bright victory.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Your Unique Design', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 18, Verse 45', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "Should I try to copy others to be successful?" Krishna shook his head and said, "Not at all, my friend. The universe made you with your own unique pattern. Doing your own simple duty with a loving heart is far better than doing someone else\'s grand job perfectly. Be happy being exactly who you are."', 'True happiness is being yourself and sharing your own unique light.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Walking Through the Garden', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 2, Verse 64', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "How can I enjoy all the nice things in the world without getting greedy or upset?" Krishna said, "Walk through the world like someone visiting a beautiful public garden, Arjuna. Enjoy the pretty colors and smell the sweet flowers with a smile, but do not try to pull them up or take them home. Enjoy things gently without needing to own them."', 'Enjoy the beautiful things in life with a free and grateful heart.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Safe Sanctuary', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 9, Verse 34', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, how do I make sure I am always acting with love?" Krishna answered gently, "Think of me with a happy smile, fill your heart with my light, and bow to the goodness in everything around you. When you anchor your thoughts in love, your whole mind becomes a beautiful, safe sanctuary where no worry can ever enter."', 'When you focus your thoughts on love, your mind becomes a safe and happy home.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Humble Question', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 4, Verse 34', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "How do I find people who can teach me the beautiful secrets of life?" Krishna smiled and said, "Look for those who are wise and calm, Arjuna. Walk up to them with a gentle smile, ask your questions with an open, humble heart, and be ready to help them. When you are ready to learn with respect, true wisdom will always find you."', 'Being humble and curious opens the door to learning wonderful new things.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Steady Horizon', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 5, Verse 20', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "What does it look like when someone has a perfectly steady mind?" Krishna pointed to the sky where the earth meets the horizon and said, "They do not dance wildly with joy when something nice happens, and they do not fall into heavy sadness when something difficult happens. They stay completely steady, clear, and peaceful, just like the beautiful horizon."', 'True peace means staying calm and balanced through life\'s small surprises.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Jewel of Calmness', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 18, Verse 42', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, what are the traits of a person who brings peace wherever they go?" Krishna answered softly, "They are masters of their own thoughts, Arjuna. They keep their body and senses gentle, they love cleanliness, they forgive others easily, they are honest, and they hold a deep trust in the wisdom of the universe. They are a true jewel of calmness."', 'Honesty, forgiveness, and self-control make you a shining light of peace.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Spark of Cleverness', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 7, Verse 10', [2], 'Arjuna watched a little bird build a beautiful, intricate nest and asked, "Where does that amazing skill come from?" Krishna smiled and whispered, "I am the clever intelligence inside the intelligent, Arjuna. I am the bright strength inside the strong. Whenever you see someone solve a problem or build something beautiful, you are seeing a small spark of my light."', 'Your clever mind and creative skills are beautiful gifts from the universe.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Free Traveler', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 6, Verse 24', [3], 'Arjuna asked, "How do I let go of all the heavy plans and expectations that make me feel stuck?" Krishna said, "Drop the heavy bags of constant wanting, Arjuna. Let go of all the complex daydreams that try to control tomorrow. Use your calm, clear mind to gently hold your thoughts still, and walk forward like a free traveler who enjoys the present moment."', 'Letting go of the need to control everything makes your heart feel light and free.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Spirit of Success', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 10, Verse 36', [3], 'Arjuna felt a sudden wave of self-doubt and asked, "Will I find the strength to cross this big challenge?" Krishna looked at him with absolute confidence and said, "I am the bright victory in every success, Arjuna! I am the unshakeable determination in every brave heart, and I am the goodness in good people. Take a deep breath—that same spirit of success lives inside you right now."', 'You carry the spirit of determination and bright victory inside your heart.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Quiet Forest Path', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 12, Verse 19', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "What is the secret of someone who feels at home anywhere they go?" Krishna replied, "It is the one who treats quiet moments and busy moments with the same calm heart, Arjuna. They are happy with whatever comes their way, they don\'t look for praise, and they carry a silent peace inside them. To a person like that, the whole world is a cozy home."', 'When you carry peace inside your heart, you are at home wherever you go.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Sweet Oasis', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 2, Verse 65', [1], 'Arjuna asked, "What happens to our daily worries when we find this inner peace?" Krishna touched his forehead and said, "In that state of sweet peace, Arjuna, all your sorrows and heartaches completely disappear. Your intellect becomes perfectly clear and steady, like a cool, sweet oasis in the middle of a dry desert, keeping you completely refreshed."', 'True inner peace melts away all sorrows, leaving your mind clean and refreshed.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Silk Ribbon of Joy', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 14, Verse 9', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, how does choosing goodness change our daily life?" Krishna smiled and explained, "Goodness is like a beautiful silk ribbon, Arjuna. It gently binds your mind to pure happiness and wraps your heart in sweet comfort. It keeps you connected to happy stories, healthy habits, and bright, joyful thoughts all day long."', 'Choosing kind and good paths naturally wraps your life in pure happiness.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Fragrance of the Earth', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 7, Verse 9', [1, 2], 'Arjuna breathed in the fresh air and asked, "Krishna, how do I notice your presence in the simple ground we walk on?" Krishna smiled and said, "I am the pure, sweet fragrance of the wet earth, Arjuna. I am also the warm heat inside the blazing fire, and the silent life force that keeps every single living being moving."', 'The magic of life is beautifully woven into the earth and everything around us.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The First Sound', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 10, Verse 33', [1, 2], 'Arjuna listened to the quiet sounds around them and asked, "How do you show up in our language and words, Krishna?" Krishna whispered softly, "Among all the letters of the alphabet, Arjuna, I am the very first sound—the letter \'A\'. I am also the endless timeline of life, looking after everything with a face of love."', 'Every beautiful thought and every kind word begins with a single spark of love.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Light Beyond Darkness', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 13, Verse 17', [1], 'Arjuna looked into a dark valley and asked, "Can any shadow or dark night ever hide the divine spirit, Krishna?" Krishna shook his head and said, "I am the light of all lights, Arjuna, sitting completely beyond any shadow or darkness. This beautiful, bright wisdom lives right inside your own heart, waiting quietly to guide you."', 'No matter how dark or scary things feel, a bright light always lives inside you.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Mind Among the Senses', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 10, Verse 22', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, how do I find your steady presence inside my own busy body?" Krishna explained, "Among all your different senses that see, hear, and touch, Arjuna, I am the clever mind that keeps them all working together. Inside every living creature, I am the glowing spark of consciousness that keeps them awake and alive."', 'Your mind is a beautiful gift that connects all your senses to the world.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Doing Your Best Freely', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 3, Verse 19', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "How do I make sure my daily actions lead me to true happiness?" Krishna answered gently, "Always do your daily tasks beautifully, Arjuna, simply because they are the right things to do. When you work with a happy heart without desperately clinging to rewards, you reach the highest state of peace."', 'Doing your best with a pure, unselfish heart is its own beautiful reward.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Equal Friend', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 9, Verse 29', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, do you love some people more than others?" Krishna looked at him with great warmth and said, "I am completely equal to all living beings, Arjuna. No one is disliked by me, and no one is a special favorite. But those who live with love in their hearts naturally live right inside me, and I live inside them like a close friend."', 'The universe loves everyone equally, and love brings us closer together.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Free from Wanting', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 12, Verse 17', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "What is the secret to keeping my heart perfectly peaceful all day long?" Krishna answered, "It belongs to the one who does not wildly celebrate when things go well, and does not cry when things go wrong, Arjuna. A person who does not grieve over the past and does not anxiously crave the future is truly dear to peace."', 'True peace is found when you let go of constant wanting and enjoy the present moment.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Supreme Home', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 18, Verse 62', [3], 'Arjuna felt the heavy weight of his responsibilities and asked, "Where can I run to when I need absolute rest?" Krishna put a protective hand on his arm and said, "Surrender all your worries to the loving power running this universe, Arjuna. By its gentle grace, you will instantly find supreme peace and an eternal, cozy home where you are always safe."', 'When you trust the universe completely, you find a permanent home of peace.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Golden Shield of Goodness', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 14, Verse 14', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "What happens to a soul that spends its time thinking beautiful, pure thoughts?" Krishna answered comfortingly, "When a person lives and breathes in pure goodness, Arjuna, their spirit rises naturally to the spotless, bright worlds where the happiest and wisest beings live, wrapped in a golden shield of light."', 'Keeping your thoughts pure and good always leads your life to a beautiful place.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Intelligent Treasure', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 18, Verse 70', [3], 'As their wonderful conversation drew to a close, Arjuna asked, "How will our talk today help others in the future?" Krishna smiled with great satisfaction and said, "Whoever studies or reads aloud this sacred, loving conversation between us is worshiping with their bright intelligence. They are filling their mind with the greatest treasure of truth."', 'Sharing wise and loving conversations fills your mind with the ultimate treasure.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Wind and the Boat', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 2, Verse 67', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, how can just one small, wandering thought cause so much trouble?" Krishna pointed to a boat on the water and said, "Think of a boat gliding on a lake, Arjuna. If a sudden, strong gust of wind blows against it, it can push the boat completely off its safe course. That is why you must gently watch your senses, so a single worry doesn\'t sweep your calm mind away."', 'Gently guide your thoughts so little worries don\'t push you off your peaceful path.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Light Heart', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 3, Verse 30', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "How can I do my daily work without feeling heavy or tired on the inside?" Krishna smiled and said, "Offer all your daily actions to me with a beautiful, light heart, Arjuna. Let go of selfishness, take a deep breath, and stand up tall without any inner fever or worry. When you work for the joy of giving, your heart stays completely free."', 'When you do your work with a generous heart, you never feel heavy or tired.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Shared Fire', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 4, Verse 24', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, how can I see the divine spirit in the ordinary things I do every day?" Krishna explained gently, "Think of a warm family meal, Arjuna. The wholesome food, the act of cooking, the warm fire, and the person enjoying the meal are all part of the exact same beautiful universal energy. Everything is connected in one big circle of love."', 'Every ordinary part of your day is connected to a grand, loving universe.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Happy Contentment', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 4, Verse 22', [1], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, who is the person who feels truly happy on the inside?" Krishna answered, "It is the one who is perfectly satisfied with whatever comes their way naturally, Arjuna. They don\'t feel jealous of anyone else, and they stay calm and smiling whether they win a game or lose it. They are always free."', 'True happiness means being happy with what you have without comparing yourself to others.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Busy Tree', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 4, Verse 18', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "How is it possible to find absolute stillness when there is so much work to do?" Krishna pointed to a large banyan tree and said, "Look at the tree, Arjuna. On the outside, it sits perfectly still, yet inside, its roots and sap are actively working to grow leaves. A wise person is just like that—they can sit peacefully inside their heart even while their hands are busy working."', 'You can keep a quiet, peaceful heart even when your hands are busy.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Wave of Anger', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 5, Verse 23', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "What makes a person truly strong right now?" Krishna answered softly, "The truly strong person is the one who can feel a big wave of anger or rushing desire come into their body, but takes a deep, calm breath and lets it pass by without letting it shake their beautiful smile. They are the true masters of their own joy."', 'Real strength means taking a deep breath and letting angry feelings pass right by.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Closest Best Friend', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 5, Verse 29', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Where can I find the ultimate comfort when the world feels too big and scary?" Krishna put a comforting hand on his shoulder and whispered, "Remember this secret, my friend: the great power that looks after all the worlds is also the closest, sweetest best friend to every single creature. You are always resting in the lap of a friend."', 'The universe is your kindest best friend, always watching over you with love.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Untying the Knot', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 6, Verse 23', [3], 'Arjuna asked, "What is the true meaning of connecting with our inner peace?" Krishna smiled warmly and said, "It means gently untying the heavy knot that binds your heart to sadness and fear, Arjuna. It is a beautiful state of safety where pain can no longer hold your hand, leaving you completely free to smile."', 'Inner peace means letting go of sadness so your heart can feel completely free.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Pure Strength', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 7, Verse 11', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, what kind of power makes the universe happy?" Krishna answered, "I am the bright strength inside strong people that is used to help, protect, and lift others up, Arjuna. I am not the power that bullies or shows off. I am the pure, gentle energy that helps life grow beautifully and safely."', 'True power is gentle and is always used to protect and help others.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Four Visitors', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 7, Verse 16', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Who are the ones who call out to the universe for comfort and love?" Krishna answered happily, "Four kinds of good people come to me, my friend: those who are having a hard day and need a hug, those who want to learn new things, those looking for comfort, and the wise who love me simply for who I am. I welcome them all with the same open arms."', 'No matter why you look for love, the universe is always ready to welcome you.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Gentle Breeze', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 9, Verse 4', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, how can you be everywhere around us if we cannot see you with our eyes?" Krishna smiled and said, "Think of the gentle morning breeze, Arjuna. You cannot see the air with your eyes, but you can feel its cool, soft touch on your face, and you see the leaves dancing on the trees. In the exact same way, my love is wrapped all around you, keeping you cool and safe even if it is invisible."', 'Just because you cannot see love with your eyes doesn\'t mean it isn\'t holding you safely.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The King of Birds', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 10, Verse 30', [2, 3], 'Arjuna looked up at the sky and asked, "How do we see your strength in the creatures of the world?" Krishna pointed upward and said, "Among all the birds that fly through the sky, Arjuna, I am the magnificent eagle Garuda, soaring high above the clouds with strong wings and a brave heart. Look at the sky and remember that you have the same strength inside you to rise above any problem."', 'You have a brave heart and strong wings inside you to rise above any difficult day.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Clean Temple', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 17, Verse 14', [1], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, what is the best way to respect and look after my physical body?" Krishna answered gently, "Treat your body like a clean, beautiful temple, my friend. Keep it clean, speak only kind words, be completely honest and simple in your actions, and never try to hurt any living being. When you look after your temple, the bright light inside it shines even brighter."', 'Keeping your actions simple and your body clean makes your inner heart shine brightly.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Infinite Blanket', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 11, Verse 15', [1, 2], 'Arjuna looked out at the massive universe and felt a little overwhelmed, asking, "Krishna, how big is your real form?" Krishna touched his eyes and said, "If you could see the whole picture, Arjuna, you would see all the stars, all the planets, all the oceans, and every single living creature resting safely inside me like patterns woven onto one grand, infinite blanket. No matter how big the world feels, you are always tucked safely inside it."', 'You are never lost or small because you are a beautiful part of a massive, loving universe.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Smooth Flow', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 18, Verse 23', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "What is the most beautiful way to complete my chores every day?" Krishna answered, "Do your work smoothly and calmly, Arjuna, without any anger, without trying to show off, and without worrying about whether people will praise you or not. When you do your daily work simply because it is a good thing to do, your actions flow as smoothly as a peaceful river."', 'Doing your work calmly and without looking for praise makes your day peaceful and smooth.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Unborn Spark', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 2, Verse 20', [1], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, where did the life inside us come from, and will it ever disappear?" Krishna looked at him with great comfort and said, "The beautiful life force inside you was never born, and it can never fade away, Arjuna. It is completely ancient, eternal, and fresh every single day. Even as your body grows and changes, the happy spark inside you stays perfectly whole and safe forever."', 'Your true inner self is eternal, timeless, and always perfectly safe.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Gentle Witness', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 9, Verse 18', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, who are you to me when I am sitting all by myself in the quiet room?" Krishna whispered softly, "I am your ultimate path, your kind caretaker, your master, and the gentle witness who sits right beside you. I am your safe house, your closest refuge, and the truest friend who never leaves your side for even a single second."', 'You are never truly alone, because a gentle friend is always watching over you with love.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Great Elephant', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 10, Verse 27', [2, 3], 'Arjuna looked at the heavy animals in the valley and asked about strength. Krishna smiled and said, "Among all the magnificent kings and animals, Arjuna, I am the great, gentle white elephant Airavata. He walks with slow, steady, and royal steps, carrying immense strength without ever losing his calm peace. Walk with that same steady, royal patience every day."', 'True power means moving through life with slow, steady, and peaceful steps.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Unshaken Rock', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 6, Verse 22', [3], 'Arjuna asked, "What happens when someone is completely anchored in their inner joy?" Krishna answered with absolute certainty, "When you find that beautiful spot of joy inside your heart, Arjuna, you realize nothing in the world is more precious. You become so solid and grounded that even if a massive storm of heavy sorrow or physical pain blows against you, it cannot shake your peace."', 'When you are full of inner joy, no outside storm can shake your steady strength.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Nourishing Soil', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 15, Verse 13', [1, 2], 'Arjuna looked at the green grass and asked, "How does the earth look after all these tiny plants so beautifully?" Krishna explained, "I enter the rich, dark soil of the earth, Arjuna, and sustain every living plant with my warm energy. I become the sweet, watery moon that feeds all the delicious fruits and vegetables, helping them grow juicy and full of life for you."', 'The universe is constantly feeding and nourishing you with everything you need to grow strong.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Campfire of Wisdom', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 4, Verse 37', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, how can I clear away a big pile of old mistakes or heavy worries that make my heart feel crowded?" Krishna pointed to a warm campfire and said, "Look at how a roaring, bright fire turns a massive heap of heavy wooden logs into soft, light, and harmless ash in just a few moments. The bright fire of true inner wisdom does the exact same thing—it instantly burns away all your past worries, leaving your heart perfectly clean and light."', 'True wisdom burns away all your past worries, leaving your heart clean and free.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Three Colored Threads', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 14, Verse 5', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, why does my body feel full of peaceful light on some days, wildly restless on other days, and completely heavy or lazy on some mornings?" Krishna explained gently, "Nature has three different colored threads that weave through our days, Arjuna: a bright white thread of peace, a red thread of rushing around, and a dark thread of feeling heavy. When you take a deep breath and stay calm, you can gently choose to hold onto the peaceful white thread."', 'You can always take a deep breath and choose your way back to a peaceful state.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Safe Haven', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 9, Verse 33', [1], 'Arjuna looked around at the world and asked, "What should I do when everything outside feels temporary, constantly changing, and full of shifting rules?" Krishna looked at him with absolute comfort and said, "Since this world is full of quick changes and temporary moments, just turn inward and rest in my arms of love. I am your safe, unshakeable haven where nothing can ever hurt you, and you will always find perfect joy."', 'Love is a safe, unchanging shelter where you can always rest your heart.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Great Wheel of Giving', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 3, Verse 10', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, what is the secret to how this beautiful world keeps running so smoothly every single day?" Krishna smiled and explained, "The universe works like a great, beautiful wheel of giving, Arjuna. The fluffy clouds give rain, the rich soil gives green plants, and the trees give sweet fruit. When we share what we have and help one another with a happy smile, we are keeping the beautiful wheel of life spinning happily."', 'Sharing your joy and helping others keeps the whole world spinning happily.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Wise Scholar', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 2, Verse 11', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, how do I know when my mind is thinking with true, steady wisdom?" Krishna answered gently, "A truly wise person speaks words of helpful truth, but they never sit down to cry over things that pass away, Arjuna. They know that life is continuous, beautiful, and always safe, so they do not waste their precious energy mourning over little changes that are completely natural."', 'True wisdom keeps your heart steady and peaceful through life\'s little changes.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Room of Fresh Air', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 17, Verse 16', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "What is the best way to make my mind feel completely clean, pleasant, and happy inside my own chest?" Krishna whispered softly, "Keep your inner mind serene, practice being completely gentle with everyone you meet, enjoy quiet moments of silence, and keep your thoughts honest and pure. When you practice this, your mind becomes just like a beautiful, clean room filled with fresh air."', 'Pure, quiet thoughts make your inner mind a beautiful and happy home.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Still Arrow', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 6, Verse 18', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "What does it look like when someone has perfectly trained their focus and doesn\'t get distracted?" Krishna answered, "Think of a straight arrow resting perfectly still on the bow, completely steady before it flies, Arjuna. When your mind stops wandering after outside noises or frantic wishes, and rests quietly inside your own soul, you become completely peaceful, unshakeable, and strong."', 'When your mind rests quietly inside your own soul, you become steady and strong.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Great Canvas', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 6, Verse 29', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, how does a person look at the world when their heart is full of true peace?" Krishna explained, "A peaceful person looks at the whole world like a single, magnificent painting, Arjuna. They see their own happy soul reflecting in every living creature, and they see every living creature resting safely inside them. They recognize that we all share the exact same beautiful spirit."', 'We are all beautiful parts of the exact same loving spirit.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Carousel of Care', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 18, Verse 61', [3], 'Arjuna felt completely exhausted from trying to manage every single plan and outcome by himself. Krishna put a comforting hand on his arm and said, "The loving power of the universe lives deep inside the heart of every creature, Arjuna, gently moving this whole world like travelers sitting on a carousel. Relax your grip, trust the ride, and let that great power carry you safely."', 'Relax your grip, trust the universe, and let love carry you safely home.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Pure River', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 10, Verse 31', [1, 2], 'Arjuna took a deep breath of fresh air and asked, "Krishna, where can I feel your pure, cleansing energy when I am out in nature?" Krishna answered happily, "Among all the fast, purifying winds that sweep through the valley, I am the fresh air. And among all the grand, rushing rivers that wash the earth clean, I am the sacred river Ganges. Feel my freshness in every clean breeze and cool stream."', 'Nature’s fresh air and cool water are gifts that clean and refresh your spirit.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Sweet Little Fragment', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 15, Verse 7', [1], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, where does the bright spark of life inside a tiny, growing baby come from?" Krishna smiled with immense warmth and said, "A beautiful, eternal fragment of my very own self steps into this world to become a living soul, Arjuna. It brings life, senses, and a sweet heart into the body. That little life is a true piece of my love."', 'Every new life is a precious, eternal fragment of the universe\'s love.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Infinite Hands', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 13, Verse 14', [1, 2], 'Arjuna looked around and asked, "How can the universe look after so many things all at once?" Krishna explained, "The divine spirit has hands and feet everywhere, Arjuna. It has eyes, heads, and faces looking in every direction, and ears listening to every whisper. No matter where you go or what you do, those loving hands are always there to support and protect you."', 'The universe has infinite hands and eyes always watching over you with care.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Master of the Chariot', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 6, Verse 6', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, how do I make sure my mind helps me instead of making me feel trapped?" Krishna answered, "For the person who has learned to gently guide their thoughts, their mind becomes their greatest friend and helper, Arjuna. But if the mind is left wild and unguided, it can feel like a little enemy causing mischief inside. Be the gentle master of your thoughts."', 'When you guide your thoughts with love, your mind becomes your best helper.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Undivided Light', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 18, Verse 20', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "What is the truest kind of knowledge we can find, Krishna?" Krishna answered softly, "It is the wisdom that looks at all the countless, different creatures in the world and sees one single, undivided life force tying them all together, Arjuna. When you see that we are all made of the same light, your heart fills with absolute peace."', 'Real wisdom is seeing the one same beautiful life force inside every living being.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Gentle Form', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 11, Verse 50', [3], 'Arjuna felt frightened after seeing the vast, fiery cosmic sky and asked for comfort. Krishna instantly dissolved the giant, flashing lights, put on his beautiful, familiar clothes, and showed his gentle, smiling face again. Krishna whispered, "Do not fear, my friend. Look at my peaceful, human form. I am right here beside you, gentle, calm, and full of sweet comfort."', 'The universe is fundamentally gentle, kind, and always right here to soothe your fears.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Free Heart', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 2, Verse 57', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "How does a wise person handle things when life brings mixed surprises?" Krishna said, "A person with a steady mind is someone who is free from attachment in every situation, Arjuna. When something wonderful happens, they don\'t get boastful or wildly frantic, and when something difficult happens, they don\'t get bitter or sad. They keep a completely free and peaceful heart."', 'Keep a free and steady heart, without letting outside events control your joy.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Ultimate Caretaker', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 9, Verse 17', [1], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, what is your real relationship to this big world and to us?" Krishna looked at him with endless affection and said, "I am the father who protects, the mother who nourishes, the sustainer who holds everything together, and the kind grandfather of this entire universe, Arjuna. You are completely a part of my family."', 'You are a cherished child of a loving universe that fathers, mothers, and sustains you.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Guide of Your Steps', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 18, Verse 56', [3], 'Arjuna asked, "How can I be sure that I am safe even when I am doing hard things?" Krishna held his hand and said, "Even if you are performing difficult tasks or facing a long journey, Arjuna, if you take full shelter in my love and trust the path, you will reach an eternal, peaceful, and unchanging home by my grace."', 'Taking shelter in love ensures that every journey leads you safely home.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Spring of Kindness', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 16, Verse 2', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, what are the traits that make a house feel warm and full of good energy?" Krishna replied, "It is a place filled with truthfulness, an absence of anger, a spirit of letting go, quiet peace, and deep compassion for all living creatures, Arjuna. When you are gentle, modest, and steady, your whole house turns into a beautiful spring of kindness."', 'Gentleness, peace, and kindness turn your heart into a beautiful place to live.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Gift of Peaceful Rest', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 2, Verse 66', [3], 'Arjuna noticed his breathing was heavy and asked, "Can a person ever find true happiness if their mind is constantly racing?" Krishna shook his head gently and whispered, "For someone who cannot sit quietly or focus their thoughts, there is no inner calmness, Arjuna. And for someone who has no peace, how can there ever be true happiness? Breathe deeply, find your peace, and rest."', 'True happiness cannot live without peace, so take a deep breath and find your calm.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The First Step Never Fails', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 2, Verse 40', [1], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, what happens if I start a good path but cannot finish it? Is all my hard work wasted?" Krishna smiled warmly and shook his head, "On this beautiful path of peace, Arjuna, no effort is ever lost, and no small start is ever destroyed. Even a tiny bit of good work protects you from great fear."', 'Every single good thing you do is safe and stays with you forever.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Thread of Time', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 10, Verse 32', [1, 2], 'Arjuna looked at how quickly the days pass and asked, "Krishna, where do you live within the ticking clock of life?" Krishna answered gently, "I am the very beginning, the middle, and the absolute end of everything that is created, my friend. I am also the quiet wisdom inside a meaningful conversation."', 'The universe is with you through every phase of your journey.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Quiet Sky', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 6, Verse 27', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "What is the greatest reward for someone who calms their thoughts?" Krishna replied, "The highest joy comes to the person whose mind is perfectly peaceful, Arjuna. When your restless emotions settle down, your heart becomes as clear and bright as a quiet sky after a storm, free from any disturbances."', 'A quiet mind brings a deep, clean happiness that needs nothing else.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Your Own Path', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 3, Verse 35', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "Is it better to try to be perfect at someone else\'s job or just do my own little part?" Krishna looked at him and said, "It is always better to follow your own unique path, even if it feels small or imperfect, Arjuna. Trying to live someone else\'s life brings worry and fear. Embrace your own role with a happy smile."', 'True peace comes from being happy with your own unique journey.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Root of the Forest', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 13, Verse 30', [1, 2], 'Arjuna looked out at a forest with many different kinds of trees and asked, "How do we see unity when everything looks so separate?" Krishna answered, "When you realize that all the different creatures, plants, and people are rooted in the exact same source, you see the truth. They all branch out from the same loving ground."', 'We all come from the same loving source, making us one big family.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Pleasant Mind', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 17, Verse 16', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, what makes our inner self feel completely satisfied and light?" Krishna answered softly, "Keep your heart pleasant and cheerful, love quiet moments of peace, and let your thoughts be entirely clean and honest. This gentle control over your mind keeps your inner world beautiful."', 'Choosing cheerful, pure thoughts creates a delightful home inside you.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Golden Nectar', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 12, Verse 20', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "Who are the ones who drink the sweetest joy from your wisdom?" Krishna smiled and said, "Those who listen to these peaceful truths with deep trust, fill their hearts with love, and make the universe their ultimate goal, Arjuna. They are drinking a golden nectar of goodness, and they are incredibly dear to me."', 'Trusting in pure goodness fills your life with the sweetest joy.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Foundation of Joy', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 14, Verse 27', [3], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, what holds up the ultimate peace and happiness that never fades away?" Krishna held his hand firmly and said, "I am the solid foundation for that eternal spirit, Arjuna. I am the home of unchangeable goodness, the root of true righteousness, and the source of pure, absolute joy that lasts forever."', 'Unshakeable joy comes from leaning on the loving power of the universe.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Steady Lamp', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 10, Verse 11', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "What happens when the darkness of worry tries to sneak into my mind?" Krishna gave him a reassuring look and said, "Out of pure compassion for you, Arjuna, I shine a bright, glowing lamp of wisdom from deep within your heart. This beautiful light instantly chases away all the dark shadows of confusion."', 'The light of love inside you will always chase away any scary thought.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Open Gate', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 7, Verse 21', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Does the universe hear us when we pray or wish for help in different ways?" Krishna nodded with endless love and said, "Whichever form of goodness a person chooses to believe in with devotion, I make their faith steady and strong, Arjuna. Every gentle wish for peace is answered through an open gate of love."', 'The universe supports your faith and always answers your pure wishes.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The River of Time', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 2, Verse 13', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, why does our physical form have to change so much as we grow?" Krishna answered gently, "Just like a person passes smoothly through childhood, youth, and old age in this life, the inner soul flows continuously through every change without ever getting hurt. A steady mind accepts this beautiful flow without any fear."', 'Your inner spirit remains perfectly safe and continuous through every change.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Generous Shield', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 3, Verse 9', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "How do I make sure my daily chores do not lock me into a cycle of worry?" Krishna answered, "Do your work in a spirit of giving, Arjuna, like a beautiful gift to the world. When you act out of pure love and generosity, your work turns into a shield that protects your mind from any stress or pressure."', 'Working with a generous spirit turns daily chores into a source of peace.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Large Mirror', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 4, Verse 35', [1], 'Arjuna asked, "What happens when someone opens their eyes to true inner wisdom?" Krishna smiled and said, "When you find this light, Arjuna, you will never fall into confusion again. You will look out at all the different creatures in the universe and see them all resting safely inside your own heart, and inside my love, like a large, beautiful mirror."', 'We are all interconnected, resting safely within the same circle of love.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Golden Lantern', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 5, Verse 24', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, who is the person who lives in absolute freedom every day?" Krishna answered softly, "It is the one who finds their happiness entirely on the inside, who rejoices from within, and whose heart is illuminated by their own inner light. That person carries a golden lantern inside them and rests in perfect, divine peace."', 'True joy is found inside your own heart, not in outside things.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The True Helper', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 6, Verse 1', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "Who is the true helper of the world?" Krishna replied, "It is the person who does the work that needs to be done simply because it is right, without demanding rewards or praise, Arjuna. They don\'t turn away from the world; they just step forward with a quiet smile to do their best for everyone."', 'Doing the right thing with a quiet smile makes you a true helper to the world.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Shared Smile', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 6, Verse 29', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "How does a person with a beautifully trained heart look at others?" Krishna said, "They look at everyone with an equal eye, Arjuna. They see their own loving soul residing inside every living being, and they see every living being sharing the same light. When they see another person smile, they feel that smile inside themselves too."', 'A peaceful heart shares the joy and light of every living creature.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Never Lost', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 6, Verse 30', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "What is your promise to someone who sees your love in everything?" Krishna held his hand tightly and said, "For the person who sees me everywhere and sees everything resting inside my care, I am never lost to them, and they are never, ever lost to me. We stay connected like a melody and its song."', 'You are never alone because the universe\'s love is always wrapped around you.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Living in Love', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 6, Verse 31', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "How does a wise person navigate their daily life after finding this truth?" Krishna answered happily, "They realize that the same spark of life lives inside everyone, so they treat all beings with love. No matter what job they are doing or where they are walking, they are always living and breathing right inside my joyful light."', 'When you treat others with kindness, you are always living in a peaceful space.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Great Cloud', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 7, Verse 12', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, are you controlled by the changing moods and patterns of nature?" Krishna shook his head and said, "All the bright, active, and quiet states of the world come from me, Arjuna. But look at this secret: even though they come from me, I am not trapped inside them. I am like a great sky that holds the clouds but stays free."', 'You can hold your changing emotions without letting them trap your inner peace.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Healing Herb', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 9, Verse 16', [1], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, how involved are you in the simple, healing parts of our world?" Krishna whispered warmly, "I am the sacred chant, I am the beautiful offering, and I am the healing herb that grows from the earth to bring comfort. I am the sweet, clarified butter and the warm fire that cooks your nourishing meals."', 'The universe provides sweet, healing elements all around us to keep us healthy.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Great Fountain', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 10, Verse 8', [1], 'Arjuna looked at the grand mountains and asked, "Where does all of this creation burst out from?" Krishna smiled and said, "I am the great, joyful fountain from which all things originate, Arjuna. Everything in this entire universe flows out from my imagination. Knowing this, the wise fill their hearts with devotion and adore the beauty of life."', 'Every beautiful part of creation flows out from a single fountain of love.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Shared Sparks', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 10, Verse 9', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "What do your close friends talk about when they sit together in quiet moments?" Krishna answered happily, "Their minds are entirely focused on love, and their lives are dedicated to peace. They sit together, lighting up each other\'s hearts by sharing wise stories and talking about goodness, finding constant delight and satisfaction."', 'Surrounding yourself with kind words and happy stories keeps your heart delighted.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('Three Kinds of Love', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 11, Verse 44', [3], 'Arjuna felt a little overwhelmed and asked for a gentle connection. Krishna stepped close and whispered, "I am right here beside you, Arjuna. I hold you gently, just like a loving father holds his little child, just like a loyal best friend walks with his friend, and just like a dear protector wraps their arms around their beloved."', 'The universe loves you with the deep care of a father, a best friend, and a protector.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Kind Neighbor', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 12, Verse 13', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "How do I become a true comfort to the people around me?" Krishna answered, "Be like a kind neighbor to all of life, Arjuna. Do not carry any dislike in your heart, be friendly and full of soft compassion to every creature, let go of thinking \'this is mine,\' and stay balanced and smiling whether you experience joy or pain."', 'Soft compassion and a friendly smile make your heart a comfortable home for everyone.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Secret Treasure', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 13, Verse 13', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "What is the ultimate secret treasure that we should all try to understand?" Krishna answered softly, "It is the ancient spark of life that has no beginning and no end, Arjuna. It sits beyond what is seen and unseen, holding a beautiful light that can never be turned off. When you understand this treasure, you find timeless peace."', 'Deep inside you lies a timeless treasure of life that is always safe.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Glowing Palace', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 14, Verse 11', [2, 3], 'Arjuna asked, "How can I tell when my body and mind are completely tuned to pure goodness?" Krishna answered with a bright smile, "When the bright light of wisdom streams out from every gateway of your body—from your eyes, your words, and your gentle actions—you will know that your inner self is resting inside a glowing palace of peace."', 'When your mind is full of goodness, your whole body radiates a warm, healthy light.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Warm Tummy Fire', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 15, Verse 14', [1], 'Arjuna asked, "Krishna, how do you look after our physical health on the inside?" Krishna explained gently, "I live inside the bodies of all breathing creatures as a warm, comforting digestive fire. Working together with the gentle incoming and outgoing breaths, I digest the nourishing food you eat, turning it into rich health and energy."', 'A gentle warmth inside you works with your breath to turn food into healthy energy.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Inner Library', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 15, Verse 15', [2], 'Arjuna asked, "Where do my quiet memories and sudden good ideas come from?" Krishna touched his chest and whispered, "I am seated deep inside the heart of everyone, Arjuna. From me comes the clear memory to remember love, the beautiful wisdom to make good choices, and the peaceful ability to let go of things you no longer need."', 'Your heart is an inner library that always holds the wisdom and love you need.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The House of Belief', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 17, Verse 3', [1, 2], 'Arjuna asked, "What shapes the real character of a person, Krishna?" Krishna answered, "A person is completely shaped by what they choose to believe in their heart, Arjuna. We live inside the house of our own faith. If you fill your faith with gentle, beautiful, and kind thoughts, your whole life becomes magnificent."', 'Fill your heart with beautiful beliefs, because you become what you choose to trust.'),
  GarbhSacredStory('The Clear Mind', 'Bhagavad Gita, Chapter 18, Verse 73', [3], 'At the very end of their conversation, Arjuna took a deep breath, stood up tall, and said with a brave smile, "Krishna, by your gentle grace, all my confusion has melted away. I remember who I truly am, my mind is completely clear and steady, and I am ready to walk forward without any doubts."', 'Remembering who you are makes you perfectly steady and ready for any journey.'),
];
